    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CLCXcowaFWRUVhgwvcQUkh)_\n\n## What\n- `vulpea-db-autosync-mode` was already started by an idle timer from `emacs-startup-hook`, but only after 30 idle seconds, and with no guard. Using `sp-find-note` before that left the picker without autosync.\n- `sp-vulpea-start-autosync` is now idempotent: cancels the pending timer, does nothing if the mode is already on.\n- New `sp-vulpea-schedule-autosync` sets the idle timer; runs at once if init is already over (e.g. module reload).\n- `sp-vulpea-autosync-delay` (defcustom, now `number`) defaults to 10 s instead of 30.\n- `sp-find-note` calls `sp-vulpea-start-autosync` first.\n- Docs updated: `sp-vulpea.org`, `sp-org-tag-groups.org`.\n\n## Freeze check\n- Enabling the mode only starts the background scan (`vulpea-db-sync-scan-on-enable` = `'background`); the select-cache prewarm stays off (#270). The enable message reports its duration.\n- Risk: #270 raised the delay to 30 s while chasing a start-up hang. If 10 s hangs, raise the defcustom.\n\n## Testing (not run in Emacs; none in the container)\n1. Start Emacs, wait ~10 s idle: `[vulpea] starting autosync...` appears in `*Messages*`; `vulpea-db-autosync-mode` is `t`.\n2. Start Emacs and press `M-o f` at once: autosync starts before the picker opens.\n3. Edit and save a note's title, `M-o f`: the new title is listed.\n4. `M-x sp-vulpea-start-autosync` twice: second call does nothing.\n5. `M-x customize-variable sp-vulpea-autosync-delay`, set 3, restart: starts after 3 idle seconds.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy owns them).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiA7r7r3sa29MoBd8wt)_",
